#op: bind-filled
#path: lineages.ship
A lineage compiled on its own is filled into a larger value with `FillPath`
and bound from there. The result is a value built in Go: CUE keeps no build
instance for it, so bind cannot tell the lineage's own declarations from the
value around it, and refuses it. `thema.Compose` writes the lineage into the
larger value's package as a file instead, and the package loaded from those
files binds. A field of a loaded package, passed instead of the package's
root and the path to the field, is refused the same way.
-- holder.cue --
lineages: ship: _
-- lineage.cue --
name: "ship"
schemas: "0": "0": schema: {a?: string}
-- out/json --
{
  "diagnostics": [
    {
      "code": "E0152",
      "severity": "error",
      "headline": "a lineage is bound from the root of a value CUE built from source, and this root was built in Go",
      "notes": [
        {
          "label": "bind tells the lineage's own declarations from the CUE around it by the build instance of the root it is bound from, and a value made by FillPath or Unify has none"
        }
      ],
      "help": [
        "compose separately built lineages into one package with thema.Compose, load it, and bind each lineage from that package's root"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "summary": {
    "errors": 1,
    "warnings": 0,
    "notes": 0
  }
}
